{
 "_notes": "v2 (2026-10-06, after the v1 mix raised human creative/expository/news scores on benchmark-v3): keep ALL windows of each heterogeneous mixed document (human-only, mixed and AI) so every domain carries its natural human:AI balance; drop the separate human controls, whose text duplicates the mixed documents' human windows. GRADTEX spans, NASA/NOAA human windows, the Beige Book/WikiText drops and the leakage list are unchanged. v1 kept only AI-containing windows of mixed documents (1,450/shard) against 1,020 control windows, which skewed fiction and old-paper windows toward AI. Revisions before launch: (1) v14 GRADTEX 'span' rows turned out to be human seed text only (all label 0), so they are dropped (redundant with base GRADTEX); no short-span AI supply remains. (2) JMLR mixed documents are AI-majority by construction (0.80:1 human:AI chars without controls), so 300 JMLR control windows per shard are added. (3) Curly quotes in the NASA/NOAA human rows are straightened (1:1, offsets unchanged), matching the heterogeneous-ai-spans v1.4.0 rule.",
 "stage1": {
  "include": false,
  "notes": "Stage 1 unchanged (12,000 rows). Keeps the A/B difference to stage 2 and avoids doubling exposure of a small pool."
 },
